---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="LLM Provider Partnership — Value Proposal"
  description="What the Poesis stack brings to LLM capabilities — and what LLMs bring to Poesis. Models propose; humans dispose through ITIP; SIE evaluates and enforces governed constraints."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Partnerships</p>
      <h1>LLM Provider Partnership — Value Proposal</h1>
      <p class="lead"><strong>Better context beats bigger models.</strong> Frontier models reason against statistical traces of the world — not against an explicit, causal, governed model of it. That single gap drives both of today's ceilings: the <a href="#capability-ceiling"><strong>capability ceiling</strong></a> and the <a href="#deployment-ceiling"><strong>deployment ceiling</strong></a>. Poesis closes both through one governed definition layer implemented across GSM, SIE, and domain platforms such as ITIP — and model providers are the natural partners on it.</p>
      <p class="lead"><strong>Models propose. Humans dispose through ITIP. SIE evaluates and enforces governed constraints.</strong> Every model output remains a proposal until accountable humans validate it against the governed definition layer.</p>
      <div class="reference-disclosure">
        <strong>How to read this proposal.</strong> Present tense describes the Poesis reference design and target operating model; it does not imply uniform implementation maturity. The maturity disclosures below distinguish implemented foundations, designed components, partnership implementation tracks, and longer-horizon work.
      </div>
      <div class="hero-cta">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact">Talk to us</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/gsm">The GSM standard</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/sie">The SIE engine</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--soft">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">The partnership thesis</p>
      <h2>Five reasons to partner.</h2>
      <p class="lead">One partnership addresses two limits: governed context raises the <a href="#capability-ceiling"><strong>capability ceiling</strong></a>; governed execution, market access, platform advantage, and sovereignty raise the <a href="#deployment-ceiling"><strong>deployment ceiling</strong></a>.</p>
      <div class="thesis-grid">
        <div class="card card--feature" id="capability-ceiling">
          <span class="tag">Capability ceiling</span>
          <h3>Better intelligence without bigger models.</h3>
          <p>A model that trains and reasons against causal, governed Definitions works against explicit structure rather than relying only on correlation. That structure provides a substrate for impact analysis, counterfactual testing, and planning against modeled dependencies.</p>
          <p class="thesis-mechanisms"><strong>Supported by adherence</strong> B · Governed inference grounding</p>
          <p class="thesis-tagline">Don't compete on larger models. Compete on better intelligence.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card card--feature" id="deployment-ceiling">
          <span class="tag">Deployment ceiling · Enterprise platform</span>
          <h3>From model provider to enterprise AI platform.</h3>
          <p>Companies buy solutions, not models. Partner models provide the intelligence; Poesis provides governed context, business rules, human disposition, deterministic evaluation, and accountability. Together they form a deployable enterprise agentic platform — able to act, not only answer.</p>
          <p class="thesis-mechanisms"><strong>Supported by adherences</strong> B · Governed inference grounding + C · Governed inference deployment</p>
          <p class="thesis-tagline">Transform a model into an enterprise AI platform.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card card--feature">
          <span class="tag">Deployment ceiling · Market access</span>
          <h3>A credible path into regulated industries.</h3>
          <p>Enterprises don't stall because AI isn't powerful enough — they stall because they can't trust it to act. Explainability, governance, auditability, and policy enforcement are entry conditions, and Poesis is designed to provide their shared context and control substrate.</p>
          <p class="thesis-mechanisms"><strong>Supported by adherence</strong> C · Governed inference deployment</p>
          <p class="thesis-tagline">Governance is the entry ticket to regulated industries.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card card--feature">
          <span class="tag">Deployment ceiling · Platform advantage</span>
          <h3>A defensible advantage beyond model performance.</h3>
          <p>Grounded inference, governed execution, and model specialisation create a combined platform that is harder to commoditize than standalone inference. It moves the commercial relationship into AI governance, digital operating models, enterprise transformation, and regulated automation — increasing deal scope and strategic relevance.</p>
          <p class="thesis-mechanisms"><strong>Supported by adherences</strong> B · Governed inference grounding + C · Governed inference deployment + D · Model specialisation</p>
          <p class="thesis-tagline">Build a platform advantage, not simply a model advantage.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card card--feature">
          <span class="tag">Deployment ceiling · Sovereignty</span>
          <h3>The foundation of a sovereign AI stack.</h3>
          <p>Not "a sovereign LLM" — a sovereign AI <em>stack</em>. You provide the sovereign intelligence. Poesis provides the governed context. Together they form the trusted infrastructure enterprises need to deploy AI at scale. As a neutral, model-independent substrate, GSM/SIE could be advanced as a candidate foundation for future European standardization of governed enterprise AI.</p>
          <p class="thesis-mechanisms"><strong>Supported by adherences</strong> A–E · The complete governed AI value cycle</p>
          <p class="thesis-tagline">Build the sovereign AI stack, not only a sovereign model.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">The value mechanisms / adherences</p>
      <h2>How the partnership creates value.</h2>
      <p class="lead">Each business outcome is supported by one or more mechanisms connecting LLM capabilities with the Poesis stack, each forming a locus of value adherence.</p>
      <div class="value-grid">
        <button class="card value-card" data-flow="A" type="button">
          <span class="tag">Context sourcing · A</span>
          <h3>Definitions sourced at scale</h3>
          <p>LLMs can become KnowledgeSources over repositories, wikis, ticketing systems, and authoritative resources — lowering sourcing cost while preserving human disposition.</p>
          <span class="value-link">Show adherence →</span>
        </button>
        <button class="card value-card" data-flow="B" type="button">
          <span class="tag">Governed inference loop · B</span>
          <h3>Governed causal grounding</h3>
          <p>SIE supplies structurally causal, governed, rights-traceable Definitions and tools that let models reason beyond document-only retrieval and trace modeled dependencies.</p>
          <span class="value-link">Show adherence →</span>
        </button>
        <button class="card value-card" data-flow="C" type="button">
          <span class="tag">Governed inference loop · C</span>
          <h3>Governed action in regulated estates</h3>
          <p>Models propose; humans dispose through ITIP; SIE evaluates deterministically. The result is accountable agentic action with evidence behind every decision.</p>
          <span class="value-link">Show adherence →</span>
        </button>
        <button class="card value-card" data-flow="D" type="button">
          <span class="tag">Model specialisation · D</span>
          <h3>A legitimate specialisation substrate</h3>
          <p>Governed Definitions and Ascription history provide a provenance-rich, rights-governed corpus and a basis for an evaluation oracle unavailable from ungoverned scraping alone.</p>
          <span class="value-link">Show adherence →</span>
        </button>
        <button class="card value-card" data-flow="E" type="button">
          <span class="tag">Agentic delivery · E</span>
          <h3>A governed agentic delivery proof</h3>
          <p>Partner models power specialist agents while deterministic SAFe operational gates and human approvals govern how organisation products are delivered.</p>
          <span class="value-link">Show adherence →</span>
        </button>
      </div>

      <div class="maturity-panel" id="maturity">
        <p class="eyebrow">Maturity disclosure</p>
        <h3>The reference design is stable; its operational maturity is evolving.</h3>
        <p>Implementation is part of the partnership exchange, not a hidden prerequisite. A partner can contribute model access, engineering, evaluation, and applied research to turn selected flows into measured operational proofs.</p>
        <div class="maturity-grid">
          <article>
            <span class="maturity-code">A · Partnership implementation track</span>
            <p>The Blackboard and repository-sourcer contracts are designed. The service lifecycle, KnowledgeSources, client reduction, and Definition Manager registration path remain implementation and experimentation work.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="maturity-code">B · Integration and evaluation track</span>
            <p>GSM, the Definition Manager, and the SIE Operator provide foundations. The model-facing context/tool surface and comparative grounding benchmarks are partnership work.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="maturity-code">C · Target composition</span>
            <p>The governance lifecycle and deterministic runtime foundations exist. The integrated ITIP human gate, Norm and provenance evaluation, disposition audit, and regulated-estate proof remain to be assembled and validated.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="maturity-code">D · Research track</span>
            <p>GSM provides governed structural definitions and versioned Ascriptions. Corpus permissions, evaluation-oracle construction, specialization experiments, and measured uplift require explicit partner and tenant agreements.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="maturity-code">E · Evolving operational proof</span>
            <p>The SAFe Agentic Framework supplies the delivery pattern and artifacts. Partner-model adoption, controlled execution evidence, and repeatable outcome measures continue to mature through use.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <div class="maturity-exchange">
          <p><strong>Direct value for Poesis:</strong> faster implementation, stronger experiments, benchmark evidence, and production feedback across the reference design.</p>
          <p><strong>Indirect value for the LLM provider:</strong> a governed enterprise integration proving where its models perform, fail, and improve under accountable operating constraints.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--soft" id="value-map">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">The value flows</p>
      <h2>An interactive map of the exchange.</h2>

      <div id="vf">
        <div class="vf-notices" aria-label="How to read the value map">
          <p class="vf-notice vf-notice-info"><strong>Explore the map.</strong> Click a flow to see its mutual value. Click an LLM or Poesis component to see every adherence it has with the other components. Expand a Poesis box for internal detail.</p>
          <p class="vf-notice vf-notice-invariant"><strong>Core invariant:</strong> models <strong>PROPOSE</strong> (inferred, confidence &lt; 1.0) · accountable humans dispose through ITIP · SIE evaluates and enforces governed constraints — <strong>PROPOSE / DISPOSE</strong>.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="vf-human">
          <strong>Human supervision, regulation, and governance — always in the loops.</strong>
          <ul>
            <li><b>Owns Intents</b> — creation of Definitions / Ascriptions.</li>
            <li><b>Owns Approvals</b> — validation of AI-proposed Definitions / Ascriptions.</li>
            <li><b>Owns Accountability</b> — evaluation and simulation of Definition / Ascription compliance and impacts, and audit of AI and human actions over Definitions / Ascriptions.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="vf-diagram" id="vf-diagram">
          <svg id="vf-wires"></svg>
          <div class="vf-cols">

            <div class="vf-col">
              <div class="vf-group" id="g-partner">
                <div class="vf-gtitle">Sovereign LLM partner</div>
                <div class="vf-gsub">provider-neutral by design — any sovereign or frontier model: self-hosted, sovereign-hosted, or open-weight</div>

                <div class="vf-card" id="n-train" data-component="Training &amp; specialisation">
                  <div class="vf-ctitle">Training &amp; specialisation</div>
                  <div class="vf-csub">learns from structurally causal, governed, rights-traceable Definitions — structured context unavailable from ungoverned scraping alone</div>
                </div>

                <div class="vf-card" id="n-infer" data-component="Grounded inference">
                  <div class="vf-ctitle">Grounded inference</div>
                  <div class="vf-csub">reasons against structurally causal, governed, rights-traceable Definitions — explicit context beyond document-only retrieval</div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="vf-gutter"></div>

            <div class="vf-col">
              <div class="vf-group" id="g-poesis">
                <div class="vf-gtitle">Poesis stack</div>
                <div class="vf-gsub">one sovereign instance per organisation — tenant-owned, designed for future federation</div>

                <div class="vf-card" id="n-sie" data-component="SIE — Systemic Intelligence Engine">
                  <div class="vf-ctitle">SIE — Systemic Intelligence Engine</div>
                  <div class="vf-csub">reference implementation of GSM containing Definitions / Ascriptions of the organisation and implementing their governance lifecycle</div>
                  <button class="vf-fold-btn" data-fold="f-sie">▸ components</button>
                  <div class="vf-fold" id="f-sie">
                    <div class="vf-comp"><b>sie-definition-manager</b> — hosts GSM, Ascription lifecycle, governance grammar</div>
                    <div class="vf-comp"><b>sie-definition-blackboard-manager</b> — Definitions sourcing pipeline</div>
                    <div class="vf-comp"><b>sie-operator</b> — executes Norms &amp; Mechanisms: governance evaluation (application of governance, and governance of governance)</div>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <div class="vf-card vf-gate" id="n-itip" data-component="ITIP — domain platform (IT)">
                  <div class="vf-ctitle">ITIP — domain platform (IT)</div>
                  <div class="vf-csub">serves the <b>PROPOSE / DISPOSE gate to humans</b> — intent, approve, audit, simulate Definitions</div>
                  <button class="vf-fold-btn" data-fold="f-itip">▸ components</button>
                  <div class="vf-fold" id="f-itip">
                    <div class="vf-comp"><b>itip web frontend + backend</b> — the human gate: intent, approval, simulation, appraisal, and audit</div>
                    <div class="vf-comp"><b>itip frameworks</b> — GDPR, NIS2, DORA, AI Act, TOGAF, ISO… standard domain vocabulary / semantics and regulation frameworks that compose GSM Definitions</div>
                    <div class="vf-comp"><b>itip blackboard sourcers</b> — wrap LLMs / agents as KnowledgeSources of Definitions over code repositories, wikis, ticketing tools, online authoritative resources, and other sources</div>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <div class="vf-card" id="n-saf" data-component="SAFe Agentic Framework">
                  <div class="vf-ctitle">SAFe Agentic Framework</div>
                  <div class="vf-csub">governed agentic organisation products delivery through deterministic operational gates</div>
                  <button class="vf-fold-btn" data-fold="f-saf">▸ components</button>
                  <div class="vf-fold" id="f-saf">
                    <div class="vf-comp"><b>orchestrators</b> — portfolio / program / team</div>
                    <div class="vf-comp"><b>specialist bench</b> — architecture, dev, QA, security, docs agents</div>
                    <div class="vf-comp"><b>harness</b> — deterministic FSM, artifact &amp; gate checks; humans approve — PROPOSE/DISPOSE applied to delivery</div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="vf-mobile-flows" role="group" aria-label="Selectable value relationships">
            <button class="vf-mobile-flow" type="button" data-flow="A" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="vf-detail">
              <span class="vf-mobile-flow-code">A · Context sourcing</span>
              <strong>Sovereign LLM partner → Poesis stack</strong>
              <span>LLM-backed sourcing of GSM</span>
            </button>
            <button class="vf-mobile-flow" type="button" data-flow="B" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="vf-detail">
              <span class="vf-mobile-flow-code">B · Governed inference grounding</span>
              <strong>Poesis stack → Sovereign LLM partner</strong>
              <span>Governed causal context + tools</span>
            </button>
            <button class="vf-mobile-flow" type="button" data-flow="C" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="vf-detail">
              <span class="vf-mobile-flow-code">C · Governed inference deployment</span>
              <strong>Sovereign LLM partner → Poesis stack</strong>
              <span>Proposals → human disposition</span>
            </button>
            <button class="vf-mobile-flow" type="button" data-flow="D" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="vf-detail">
              <span class="vf-mobile-flow-code">D · Model specialisation</span>
              <strong>Poesis stack → Sovereign LLM partner</strong>
              <span>Evaluation oracle + specialisation corpus</span>
            </button>
            <button class="vf-mobile-flow" type="button" data-flow="E" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="vf-detail">
              <span class="vf-mobile-flow-code">E · Agentic delivery</span>
              <strong>Sovereign LLM partner → Poesis stack</strong>
              <span>Agent bench builds the stack</span>
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="vf-detail" id="vf-detail" hidden></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>

<style is:global>
  .thesis-grid {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(6, 1fr); gap: 1rem; margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  .thesis-grid > .card { grid-column: span 2; }
  .thesis-grid > .card:nth-child(4) { grid-column: 2 / span 2; }

  .thesis-tagline {
    margin-top: .9rem; padding-top: .7rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--accent-ink); font-weight: 700; font-size: .95rem;
  }
  .thesis-mechanisms {
    margin-top: .9rem; padding-top: .7rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: .8rem;
  }
  .thesis-mechanisms strong { color: var(--ink); }

  .reference-disclosure {
    max-width: 920px; margin-top: 1.2rem; padding: .8rem 1rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); background: var(--accent-soft);
    color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: .9rem;
  }
  .reference-disclosure strong { color: var(--ink); }

  #vf .vf-mobile-flows { display: none; }

  .value-grid {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(6, 1fr); gap: 1rem; margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  .value-card {
    grid-column: span 2; width: 100%; color: inherit; font: inherit; text-align: left; cursor: pointer;
    transition: border-color .16s ease, box-shadow .16s ease, transform .16s ease;
  }
  .value-card:nth-child(4) { grid-column: 2 / span 2; }
  .value-card:hover, .value-card:focus-visible {
    border-color: var(--accent); box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px rgba(45, 212, 191, .14); transform: translateY(-2px); outline: none;
  }
  .value-card h3 { margin-top: .65rem; }
  .value-card p { min-height: 6.6rem; }
  .value-link { display: block; color: var(--accent-ink); font-size: .82rem; font-weight: 700; }

  .maturity-panel {
    margin-top: 2rem; padding-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
  }
  .maturity-panel h3 { max-width: 760px; margin-top: .4rem; }
  .maturity-panel > p:not(.eyebrow) { max-width: 860px; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .maturity-grid {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(6, 1fr); gap: .8rem; margin-top: 1.2rem;
  }
  .maturity-grid article {
    grid-column: span 2; padding: .85rem .95rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--line-strong);
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, .02);
  }
  .maturity-grid article:nth-child(4) { grid-column: 2 / span 2; }
  .maturity-grid p { margin: .45rem 0 0; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: .84rem; }
  .maturity-code { color: var(--accent-ink); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .76rem; font-weight: 700; }
  .maturity-exchange {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1rem; margin-top: 1rem;
    padding: .9rem 1rem; border: 1px solid rgba(56, 189, 248, .4); border-radius: 8px;
    background: rgba(56, 189, 248, .08);
  }
  .maturity-exchange p { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: .86rem; }
  .maturity-exchange strong { color: var(--ink); }

  #vf { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  #vf .vf-notices { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: .75rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  #vf .vf-notice {
    margin: 0; border-radius: 10px; padding: .65rem .85rem; font-size: .86rem; color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  #vf .vf-notice-info { background: rgba(56, 189, 248, .08); border: 1px solid rgba(56, 189, 248, .4); }
  #vf .vf-notice-invariant { background: rgba(251, 191, 36, .10); border: 1px solid rgba(251, 191, 36, .45); }
  #vf .vf-human {
    border: 1px solid rgba(251, 146, 60, .5); background: rgba(251, 146, 60, .08); border-radius: 12px;
    padding: .75rem .9rem; margin: 0 0 1.2rem;
  }
  #vf .vf-human strong { color: #fb923c; }
  #vf .vf-human ul { margin: .45rem 0 0; padding-left: 1.2rem; font-size: .84rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  #vf .vf-human li { margin-top: .2rem; }

  #vf .vf-diagram { position: relative; }
  #vf #vf-wires { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; pointer-events: none; z-index: 2; }
  #vf .vf-cols { position: relative; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 250px 1fr; z-index: 1; }
  #vf .vf-col { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem; }
  #vf .vf-gutter { pointer-events: none; }

  #vf .vf-group {
    border: 1px solid var(--line-strong); border-radius: 14px; background: var(--bg-soft);
    padding: .85rem .95rem;
  }
  #vf .vf-gtitle { font-weight: 700; color: #fff; font-size: .98rem; }
  #vf .vf-gsub { color: var(--muted); font-size: .8rem; margin-bottom: .55rem; }

  #vf .vf-card {
    border: 1px solid var(--line-strong); border-radius: 10px; background: var(--bg-ink);
    padding: .6rem .75rem; margin-top: .6rem; cursor: pointer; transition: border-color .16s ease, box-shadow .16s ease;
  }
  #vf .vf-card:hover, #vf .vf-card:focus-visible { border-color: var(--accent); box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px rgba(45, 212, 191, .12); outline: none; }
  #vf .vf-card.vf-selected { border-color: var(--accent); box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px rgba(45, 212, 191, .18); }
  #vf .vf-ctitle { font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); font-size: .89rem; }
  #vf .vf-csub { color: var(--muted); font-size: .78rem; margin-top: .18rem; }
  #vf .vf-gate { background: rgba(251, 191, 36, .07); border-color: rgba(251, 191, 36, .45); }

  #vf .vf-fold-btn {
    margin-top: .5rem; border: 1px solid var(--line-strong); background: transparent; color: var(--accent-ink);
    border-radius: 6px; font-size: .74rem; padding: .18rem .55rem; cursor: pointer;
  }
  #vf .vf-fold-btn:hover { background: var(--accent-soft); }
  #vf .vf-fold { display: none; margin-top: .55rem; border-top: 1px dashed var(--line-strong); padding-top: .55rem; }
  #vf .vf-fold.open { display: block; }
  #vf .vf-comp {
    font-size: .76rem; color: var(--ink-soft); padding: .3rem .5rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--line-strong);
    margin-top: .35rem; background: var(--bg-soft); border-radius: 0 6px 6px 0;
  }
  #vf .vf-comp b { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .72rem; color: var(--ink); }

  #vf .vf-flow-hit { pointer-events: stroke; cursor: pointer; }

  #vf .vf-detail {
    margin-top: 1.4rem; border: 1px solid var(--line-strong); border-radius: 14px;
    background: var(--bg-soft); padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
  }
  #vf .vf-detail h3 { margin: 0 0 .3rem; font-size: 1.02rem; }
  #vf .vf-maturity {
    margin: .45rem 0 .65rem; padding: .5rem .65rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    background: var(--accent-soft); color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: .8rem;
  }
  #vf .vf-maturity strong { color: var(--ink); }
  #vf .vf-dsub { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: .87rem; margin-bottom: .85rem; }
  #vf .vf-adherence + .vf-adherence { border-top: 1px solid var(--line-strong); margin-top: 1rem; padding-top: 1rem; }
  #vf .vf-adherence h4 { margin: 0 0 .3rem; font-size: .92rem; }
  #vf .vf-dcols { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1rem; }
  #vf .vf-dcols h5 { font-size: .78rem; margin: 0 0 .35rem; color: var(--muted); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .05em; }
  #vf .vf-dcols ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; font-size: .86rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  #vf .vf-dcols li { margin-bottom: .3rem; }
  #vf .vf-comps { margin-top: .9rem; font-size: .78rem; color: var(--muted); }
  #vf .vf-comps b { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .74rem; color: var(--ink); }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .thesis-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .thesis-grid > .card, .thesis-grid > .card:nth-child(4) { grid-column: auto; }
    .value-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .value-card, .value-card:nth-child(4) { grid-column: auto; }
    .value-card p { min-height: 0; }
    .maturity-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .maturity-grid article, .maturity-grid article:nth-child(4) { grid-column: auto; }
    .maturity-exchange { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    #vf .vf-notices { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    #vf .vf-cols { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    #vf .vf-gutter { display: none; }
    #vf #vf-wires { display: none; }
    #vf .vf-dcols { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    #vf .vf-mobile-flows { display: grid; gap: .65rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
    #vf .vf-mobile-flow {
      display: grid; gap: .18rem; width: 100%; min-width: 0; padding: .8rem .9rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--line-strong); border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 8px;
      background: var(--bg-soft); color: var(--ink-soft); font: inherit; font-size: .82rem;
      text-align: left; cursor: pointer; overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    }
    #vf .vf-mobile-flow:hover, #vf .vf-mobile-flow[aria-pressed="true"] {
      border-color: var(--accent); background: var(--accent-soft);
    }
    #vf .vf-mobile-flow strong { color: var(--ink); font-size: .87rem; }
    #vf .vf-mobile-flow-code { color: var(--accent-ink); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .74rem; font-weight: 700; }
  }
</style>

<script>
  const FLOWS = [
    {
      id: 'A', hex: '#38bdf8', from: 'n-infer', to: 'n-sie', lane: 32,
      label: 'LLM-backed sourcing of GSM',
      title: 'A — Context sourcing: LLMs feed GSM (LLM → Poesis)',
      maturity: 'Partnership implementation track — contracts and contribution schemas are designed; the service lifecycle, KnowledgeSources, reduction, and registration path remain to be implemented and tested.',
      sub: 'Blackboard sourcers wrap partner models as KnowledgeSources over repositories, wikis, ticketing tools, and authoritative online resources. Confidence-scored, provenance-stamped contributions form a validated sealed stream; a client reducer then prepares governed Ascription proposals for human disposition and Definition Manager registration.',
      partner: ['A concrete applied-AI showcase: turning regulation and code into governed, queryable structure', 'R&D feedback loop on extraction, grounding, function calling'],
      poesis: ['Sourcing cost down and coverage up while human disposition remains explicit', 'Invariant preserved: LLMs never write governed truth directly'],
      comps: 'Designed across <b>itip blackboard sourcers</b> → <b>sie-definition-blackboard-manager</b> → client reduction and human disposition → <b>sie-definition-manager</b>.',
    },
    {
      id: 'B', hex: '#34d399', from: 'n-sie', to: 'n-infer', lane: -32,
      label: 'governed causal context + tools',
      title: 'B — Governed inference grounding (Poesis → LLM)',
      maturity: 'Integration and evaluation track — GSM, the Definition Manager, and Operator foundations exist; the model-facing tool surface and comparative benchmarks are partnership work.',
      sub: 'SIE serves in-effect Definitions, Norms, provenance and modeled causal dependencies into the model — plus a tool surface to retrieve Definitions, inspect Norms, trace Interactions, and validate proposals.',
      partner: ['Capability edge: reasoning against explicit structure rather than correlation alone', 'Target outcome: measurably fewer unsupported claims than document-retrieval baselines'],
      poesis: ['Answers grounded in the organisation’s governed, in-effect Definitions', 'Model-neutral context standard — any conforming model can plug in'],
      comps: 'Designed through <b>sie-definition-manager</b> context and tool surfaces consumed by partner inference integrations.',
    },
    {
      id: 'C', hex: '#34d399', from: 'n-infer', to: 'n-itip', lane: 0,
      label: 'proposals → human disposition',
      title: 'C — Governed inference deployment (LLM → Poesis)',
      maturity: 'Target composition — lifecycle and deterministic runtime foundations exist; the ITIP gate, integrated Norm and provenance evaluation, disposition audit, and regulated proof remain partnership work.',
      sub: 'Every model output is a proposal. ITIP serves the PROPOSE/DISPOSE gate to humans; the SIE runtime executes Mechanisms and schema checks while governance services evaluate Norms and provenance; the target composition records every disposition for audit.',
      partner: ['Deployability: supports the controls required for agentic action in regulated estates', 'A testable assurance case for regulated European buyers'],
      poesis: ['AI that acts against the organisation\u2019s governed Definitions — audited and accountable', 'Every disposition enriches the governed record'],
      comps: 'Designed across the <b>itip web frontend + backend</b> (human gate) + <b>sie-operator</b> (Mechanism execution and schema validation) + governance evaluation and audit services.',
    },
    {
      id: 'D', hex: '#a78bfa', from: 'n-sie', to: 'n-train', lane: 0,
      label: 'evaluation oracle + specialisation corpus',
      title: 'D — Model training & specialisation substrate (Poesis → LLM)',
      maturity: 'Research track — governed structural definitions and versioned Ascriptions exist; corpus permissions, oracle construction, specialization experiments, and measured uplift require partner and tenant agreements.',
      sub: 'Governed Definitions can form an evaluation reference, while Ascription history records how accepted definitions change over time. Structural causality comes from Mechanisms and Interactions; timestamps provide temporal history, not causal proof.',
      partner: ['A differentiated specialisation corpus: structurally causal, governed, provenance-rich, and subject to explicit rights controls', 'Benchmarks against strong baselines: evidence over assertion'],
      poesis: ['Specialised sovereign models raise inference and sourcing quality — compounding every other flow', 'Legitimacy-gated access: tenant ownership absolute'],
      comps: 'Research path through <b>sie-operator</b> evaluation Mechanisms + <b>sie-definition-manager</b> governed history under explicit contractual, licensing, and consent boundaries.',
    },
    {
      id: 'E', hex: '#94a3b8', from: 'n-infer', to: 'n-saf', lane: 0, dashed: true,
      label: 'agent bench builds the stack',
      title: 'E — Agentic delivery: LLM agents build Poesis itself (LLM → Poesis)',
      maturity: 'Evolving operational proof — the delivery framework and artifacts exist; partner-model adoption, controlled execution evidence, and repeatable outcome measures mature through use.',
      sub: 'Partner models power the SAFe Agentic Framework\u2019s orchestrators and specialist bench. Agent teams deliver SIE and ITIP through deterministic harness gates with human approval — the same PROPOSE/DISPOSE invariant applied to software delivery.',
      partner: ['A living reference of governed multi-agent engineering on partner models', 'Dogfooding evidence for the enterprise agentic story'],
      poesis: ['Velocity: the stack is built by the very pattern it sells', 'Delivery traces are themselves governed, auditable artifacts'],
      comps: 'Realized by the <b>SAFe Agentic Framework</b> (orchestration layers, actor bench, deterministic harness) targeting the SIE/ITIP repos.',
    },
  ];

  const svg = document.getElementById('vf-wires');
  const diagram = document.getElementById('vf-diagram');
  const detail = document.getElementById('vf-detail');
  let selectedFlow = null;
  let selectedComponent = null;

  function anchor(el, side) {
    const r = el.getBoundingClientRect();
    const d = diagram.getBoundingClientRect();
    return { x: (side === 'right' ? r.right : r.left) - d.left, y: r.top + r.height / 2 - d.top };
  }

  function draw() {
    if (!svg || !diagram) return;
    svg.innerHTML = '';
    if (window.innerWidth <= 860) return;
    svg.setAttribute('width', String(diagram.clientWidth));
    svg.setAttribute('height', String(diagram.clientHeight));

    FLOWS.forEach((f) => {
      const fromEl = document.getElementById(f.from);
      const toEl = document.getElementById(f.to);
      if (!fromEl || !toEl) return;
      const a = anchor(fromEl, fromEl.closest('#g-partner') ? 'right' : 'left');
      const b = anchor(toEl, toEl.closest('#g-partner') ? 'right' : 'left');
      const midX = (a.x + b.x) / 2;
      const related = selectedComponent && (f.from === selectedComponent || f.to === selectedComponent);
      const sel = selectedFlow === f.id || related;

      const lane = f.lane ?? 0;
      const pathData = `M ${a.x} ${a.y} C ${midX} ${a.y + lane}, ${midX} ${b.y + lane}, ${b.x} ${b.y}`;

      const hit = document.createElementNS('http://www.w3.org/2000/svg', 'path');
      hit.setAttribute('d', pathData);
      hit.setAttribute('fill', 'none');
      hit.setAttribute('stroke', 'transparent');
      hit.setAttribute('stroke-width', '20');
      hit.setAttribute('class', 'vf-flow-hit');
      hit.setAttribute('aria-label', f.title);
      hit.addEventListener('click', () => selectFlow(f.id));
      svg.appendChild(hit);

      const p = document.createElementNS('http://www.w3.org/2000/svg', 'path');
      p.setAttribute('d', pathData);
      p.setAttribute('fill', 'none');
      p.setAttribute('stroke', f.hex);
      p.setAttribute('stroke-width', sel ? '7' : '5');
      p.setAttribute('opacity', (selectedFlow || selectedComponent) && !sel ? '0.16' : '0.82');
      p.setAttribute('pointer-events', 'none');
      if (f.dashed) p.setAttribute('stroke-dasharray', '6 5');
      svg.appendChild(p);

      const tip = document.createElementNS('http://www.w3.org/2000/svg', 'circle');
      tip.setAttribute('cx', String(b.x));
      tip.setAttribute('cy', String(b.y));
      tip.setAttribute('r', sel ? '6' : '5');
      tip.setAttribute('fill', f.hex);
      tip.setAttribute('opacity', (selectedFlow || selectedComponent) && !sel ? '0.16' : '1');
      tip.setAttribute('pointer-events', 'none');
      svg.appendChild(tip);
    });
  }

  function adherenceMarkup(flow) {
    return `<article class="vf-adherence">
      <h4 style="color:${flow.hex}">${flow.title}</h4>
      <p class="vf-maturity"><strong>Maturity:</strong> ${flow.maturity}</p>
      <p class="vf-dsub">${flow.sub}</p>
      <div class="vf-dcols">
        <div><h5>Value for the LLM partner</h5><ul>${flow.partner.map((value) => `<li>${value}</li>`).join('')}</ul></div>
        <div><h5>Value for Poesis / the customer</h5><ul>${flow.poesis.map((value) => `<li>${value}</li>`).join('')}</ul></div>
      </div>
      <div class="vf-comps">Adherence locus — ${flow.comps}</div>
    </article>`;
  }

  function showAdherences(title, flows) {
    if (!detail) return;
    detail.hidden = false;
    detail.innerHTML = `<h3>${title}</h3>${flows.map(adherenceMarkup).join('')}`;
    draw();
    detail.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'nearest' });
  }

  function clearSelection() {
    selectedFlow = null;
    selectedComponent = null;
    document.querySelectorAll('.vf-card').forEach((card) => card.classList.remove('vf-selected'));
    document.querySelectorAll('.value-card[data-flow], .vf-mobile-flow[data-flow]').forEach((control) => control.setAttribute('aria-pressed', 'false'));
    if (detail) detail.hidden = true;
    draw();
  }

  function selectFlow(id) {
    if (selectedFlow === id && !selectedComponent) {
      clearSelection();
      return;
    }
    selectedFlow = id;
    selectedComponent = null;
    document.querySelectorAll('.vf-card').forEach((card) => card.classList.remove('vf-selected'));
    document.querySelectorAll('.value-card[data-flow], .vf-mobile-flow[data-flow]').forEach((control) => {
      control.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(control.dataset.flow === id));
    });
    const flow = FLOWS.find((candidate) => candidate.id === id);
    if (!flow) {
      clearSelection();
      return;
    }
    showAdherences(`Selected value flow — ${flow.label}`, [flow]);
  }

  function selectComponent(card) {
    if (selectedComponent === card.id && !selectedFlow) {
      clearSelection();
      return;
    }
    selectedComponent = card.id;
    selectedFlow = null;
    document.querySelectorAll('.value-card[data-flow], .vf-mobile-flow[data-flow]').forEach((control) => control.setAttribute('aria-pressed', 'false'));
    document.querySelectorAll('.vf-card').forEach((candidate) => candidate.classList.toggle('vf-selected', candidate === card));
    const flows = FLOWS.filter((flow) => flow.from === card.id || flow.to === card.id);
    showAdherences(`${card.dataset.component} — ${flows.length} connected adherence${flows.length === 1 ? '' : 's'}`, flows);
  }

  document.querySelectorAll('.vf-card[data-component]').forEach((card) => {
    card.setAttribute('role', 'button');
    card.setAttribute('tabindex', '0');
    card.addEventListener('click', (event) => {
      if (event.target.closest('.vf-fold-btn')) return;
      selectComponent(card);
    });
    card.addEventListener('keydown', (event) => {
      if (event.key === 'Enter' || event.key === ' ') {
        event.preventDefault();
        selectComponent(card);
      }
    });
  });

  document.querySelectorAll('.value-card[data-flow], .vf-mobile-flow[data-flow]').forEach((control) => {
    control.addEventListener('click', () => {
      selectFlow(control.dataset.flow);
      if (control.classList.contains('value-card')) {
        document.getElementById('value-map')?.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' });
      }
    });
  });

  document.querySelectorAll('.vf-fold-btn').forEach((btn) => {
    btn.addEventListener('click', (event) => {
      event.stopPropagation();
      const fold = document.getElementById(btn.dataset.fold);
      if (!fold) return;
      fold.classList.toggle('open');
      btn.textContent = `${fold.classList.contains('open') ? '▾' : '▸'} components`;
      draw();
    });
  });

  window.addEventListener('resize', draw);
  draw();
</script>
